<!--
  Declared breaks against 1.0.0-beta.1, permitted by the repository's prerelease-stability policy and
  required by it to be declared. Two changes account for every entry here:

  1. The Affidavit as the rules define it — the record gains its two companion confidence numbers, a
     field gains a binding and a mandatory marker, and the projection port gains the entity id an
     update-shaped record needs. The positional constructors and Deconstruct members of the affected
     records change shape as a result; construction through Affidavit.Create / ProvenanceTag's
     factories is unaffected.
  2. An approval policy returns a verdict rather than a bare requirement, so it can name this write's
     review window (the deadline is stamped from the policy result, after the chain) and so the
     framework can record why a Standing Order was held back. IApprovalPolicy and
     IApprovalPolicyEvaluator change their return types; the two new members on IApprovalPolicy are
     default interface members, so an existing implementation compiles unchanged apart from the
     return type. See CHANGELOG.md's upgrade notes.
-->
